<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP_Warcasket_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); a field not discussed here is the
    Controller's. Docs/Research/VFEP_WARCASKET_STATS.md tabulates the tier.

    Tuning: VFEP's 10th-generation chassis carrying what Biotech's mechlord suit and helmet
    carry (MechBandwidth 12 each, both UltraMechtech; the suit ComponentSpacer 8,
    NanostructuringChip 2, PowerfocusChip 1). The resurrection is at or past the top of what
    vanilla and VFEP offer, so the set is gated and priced as vanilla's top tier is.
    - researchPrerequisites VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets and UltraMechtech, on all three pieces: the
      foundry lists a part by BuildableDef.IsResearchFinished, which wants every entry.
      UltraMechtech needs a NanostructuringChip analyzed, so the set comes after the first
      apocriton, whose ability the resurrector copies.
    - MechBandwidth 8, with the helmet's 12 the set's 20 against the mechlord pair's 24: the
      shell pays the suit's chips for two thirds of its bandwidth and the resurrector.
    - PsychicSensitivity -0.5, the tier's. The helmet carries none (its header), so a baseline
      pilot keeps 50% where the tier's other sets leave none; a psychically dull pilot (-0.5
      of their own) reaches zero and can take no mechlink while suited.
    - Sharp 2 / Blunt 1 / Heat 1 on all three pieces, and EnergyShieldEnergyMax 1.5 at
      EnergyShieldRechargeRate 0.01: the tier's baseline. Blunt 1.5 and the larger shields
      are other sets' specialties.
    - costList: Plasteel 150 / Uranium 50 is the tier's utility band. ComponentSpacer 8, inside
      the tier's 4 to 12, and the chips are the mechlord suit's, kept whole here because the
      resurrector is the apocriton's. Set-wide the chips are NanostructuringChip 3,
      PowerfocusChip 2 and SignalChip 2: seven boss kills spread over the apocriton, the war
      queen and the diabolus, where the mechlord pair's five chips ask the apocriton four
      times. Parts are untradeable and destroyed on drop, so their market value counts toward
      colony wealth, and through it raid points, and nothing else.
    - No apparel tags, so no pawnkind's gear roll picks the set (PawnApparelGenerator matches
      a kind's apparelTags against them): a generated pilot has no mechlink and no mechs for
      the set to serve, and the psychic sensitivity it leaves its pilot makes that pawn an
      easy capture where the tier's other sets deafen theirs. VFEP's slot fill reads no tags;
      Source/1.6/Patches/PawnGenerator_GeneratePawn_Patch_Postfix.cs keeps the set out of it.
      Save Our Ship 2's EVA tag (1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml) is then the only one a part has.

    Alpha Mechs (sarg.alphamechs) gets no compat root: it labels the vanilla chips tiers 1 to
    3 and changes nothing this set reads, so the set is its tier 3 gear. Its Mech Master
    warcasket (VFEP_Warcasket_MechController) sits behind its own tier 6 bosses, a counterpart
    rather than a peer to price against.

    Resurrect mech: VEF's CompAbilitiesApparel grants OLWC_ResurrectMech (AbilityDefs/
    ResurrectMech.xml). The ability and the sparks comp both read the mech resurrector off
    this apparel, so all three comps sit on this one def. The resurrector (Source/1.6/Comps/)
    is vanilla's CompProperties_ApparelReloadable with a recharge of its own; its props class
    sets the compClass, so none is declared here. CompDevResetCooldowns is a dev-mode cooldown
    reset (Toxin's idiom).

    The resurrector's numbers; maxCharges, chargesPerDay and ammoCountPerCharge are mod
    settings defaulting to the values here:
    - maxCharges 10, a third of the apocriton's 30. At the ability's costs of 1 / 3 / 5 / 8
      for a light, medium, heavy or ultraheavy mech that is two heavy mechs, or three medium
      and a light, or an ultraheavy and two light, in one fight; the capacity is what limits
      a fight.
    - chargesPerDay 1, the main supply, free and unattended. The vanilla route it competes
      with is the mech gestator's resurrect bills (Biotech's Recipes_MechResurrection.xml:
      25 / 50 / 100 / 150 steel and a two-day cycle, any corpse age, fully healed). A charge a
      day pays for a light mech in one day, a medium in three, a heavy in five and an
      ultraheavy in eight: slower than the gestator for all but the light, so the gestator
      keeps its place and what the resurrector adds is the mech back on its feet during the
      fight. The rate brings a resurrector spent in one raid most of the way back by the next.
    - ammoDef ComponentSpacer at ammoCountPerCharge 1, the reload: the costly shortcut for the
      raid that follows too soon or the fight that outlasts ten charges. The item is the
      Controller's, which reloads its drones with one a deployment. At 200 silver each a heavy
      or ultraheavy mech brought back on components costs about five times its gestator bill,
      so components stay the exception. Per charge rather than ammoCountToRefill, so a
      part-empty resurrector reloads for what it lacks.
    - baseReloadTicks and soundReload are the family's (the Medic's suite); chargeNoun is
      vanilla's default, spelled out because the stat sheet and the gauge's tooltip print it.

    Resurrector sparks: OLWC_ResurrectorSparks (Effects/ResurrectorSparks.xml), the
    apocriton's red crackle, on a wearer who holds a charge and could cast. onlyWhileDrafted
    true, a mod setting's default, also wants a player's pilot drafted, so the crackle reads
    as the resurrector readied for battle rather than the apocriton's constant hum.
    CompResurrectorSparks' header has the conditions.

    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/, laid out as VFEP's sets are.
    The worn graphic is Graphic_Multi (_north/_east/_south); the item icon is the parent's
    Graphic_Single, read from the bare-named file, a copy of the _south facing. The shell and
    the shoulders ship no mask, so the CompColorable colour paints the whole piece, as on the
    Controller; the helmet's header has its masks.

    Traits: traitsOnEquip grants OLWC_WarcasketTrait_Overlord rather than VFEP_WarcasketTrait,
    since a child ApparelExtension can only add to what a granted trait blocks and the
    Overlord keeps Research and Smithing open (the trait def's header). traitsOnUnequip keeps
    VFEP_Shellcasket, the "cut out of a warcasket" state every set shares, so removal surgery
    and re-entombing behave as for VFEP's own sets.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicates in a
    Def.ResolveReferences prefix, the highest priority surviving, and ApparelExtension.Merge
    does not copy every field; at equal priority the parent's copy would win. Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Patched by 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, cold insulation),
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml and the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root, which restates the piece on CE's scale; see their
    headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>OLWC_Warcasket_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, equipped with a mech resurrector that can bring recently killed mechs back to life.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, equipped with a mech resurrector that can bring recently killed mechs back to life.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The resurrector in the shell holds a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for whichever mechs are needed most at the time. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, and the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlord</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>1.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechBandwidth>8</MechBandwidth>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>8</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>150</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <NanostructuringChip>2</NanostructuringChip>
      <PowerfocusChip>1</PowerfocusChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlord</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_MechResurrector">
        <maxCharges>10</maxCharges>
        <chargesPerDay>1</chargesPerDay>
        <ammoDef>ComponentSpacer</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>charge</chargeNoun>
      </li>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_ResurrectorSparks">
        <effecterDef>OLWC_ResurrectorSparks</effecterDef>
        <onlyWhileDrafted>true</onlyWhileDrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>OLWC_ResurrectMech</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li>
        <compClass>OverlordWarcasket.CompDevResetCooldowns</compClass>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>OLWC_WarcasketTrait_Overlord</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
